From 09e29bcc8f011a06d2b941a1d3dcca17059732c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:45:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] http/qt: Send Nintendo services to a stand-in server

A new "Nintendo services" group on Configure > General > Network:
"Nintendo's servers" (default, unchanged) or "Custom server" with an
address and a switch per service:

- Connection test (conntest.nintendowifi.net)
- Game server login (nasc.nintendowifi.net), used by online games and
  the friends list
- System update check (nus.c.shop.nintendowifi.net)

http:C sends the checked services to the custom address, keeping path
and query (http when the address has no scheme, since a stand-in server
has no Nintendo certificate), with X-Tangelo-Original-Host set, and logs
each redirect. Like the SpotPass redirect this covers the online LLE
modules as well as HLE services and games.

Tangelo's SpotPass server package gets the matching service
(services/nintendo_services.py behind nginx): conntest page, NASC
LOGIN answering "server no longer available" (110) unless nasc.json
names a game server, and NUS "no update available".

New settings ([WebService], also read on Android):
use_nintendo_services_server, nintendo_services_server_url,
nintendo_services_conntest, nintendo_services_nasc, nintendo_services_nus.

